[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m reject: any of the 2^256 argument bit patterns is accepted and produces a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m result. Consequently there is no error code or sentinel to compare — the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m "same rejection" requirement degenerates into "same returned bit pattern".
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The generic C-API boundaries the task lists are structurally inapplicable
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m here and this is a property of the signature, not an assumption:
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **null pointers** — impossible: no parameter or return value is a pointer.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **zero / oversized lengths** — impossible: no length, size or count parameter.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **out-of-range enum values across FFI** — impossible: no `enum`, `int` or
