[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     33[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Input-shape axes the arithmetic actually distinguishes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     34[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     35[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `to_barycentric` has a fixed shape (exactly four `lm_vec2` = eight `float`s;
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     36[0m:[38;5;10m[49m no counts, sizes, widths, element types, formats or byte-order parameters).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     37[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The axes it *does* distinguish are therefore the numeric classes of those eight
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     38[0m:[38;5;10m[49m floats and the geometric relationships between them, because those are what
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     39[0m:[38;5;10m[49m decide the magnitude/sign/exceptional status of the intermediates
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     40[0m:[38;5;10m[49m (`v0`, `v1`, `v2`, `dot00`, `dot01`, `dot02`, `dot11`, `dot12`, `denom`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     41[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `invDenom`):
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     42[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     43[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **A. geometric relation of `p1,p2,p3`** — non-degenerate (positive area),
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     44[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   right-angled at `p1` (`dot01 == 0`), collinear (`denom == 0`), two vertices
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     45[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   coincident, all three coincident, mirrored/negative winding.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     46[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **B. position of `p`** — at `p1` (`v2 == 0`, `u = v = 0`), at `p2`, at `p3`,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     47[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   interior centroid, on an edge, outside, far outside.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     48[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **C. magnitude class** — 1, tiny (~1e-30, denom underflow), huge (~1e20,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     49[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   denom overflow), `FLT_MAX`, mixed tiny/huge in the same call.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     50[0m:[38;5;10m[49m * **D. IEEE class of individual components** — normal, `±0.0`, subnormal,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     51[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   `±inf`, quiet NaN, signalling NaN, arbitrary random bit pattern.
